  "control_findings": [
    "Official LensBlur/SR receive signed=(resized inverse depth-focus)*aperture; disparity and focus must share coordinates.",
    "Paper section3.2.2 defines aperture ratio r_target/r_max, not benchmark K/32. Public UI uses slider/10 in [0,1].",
    "The proto defaults max_aperture_radius=16 and max_kernel_radius=8 are not referenced by the interactive forward to convert benchmark K to output pixel radius.",
    "For a fixed frame span s, minmax disparity/focus plus aperture multiplied by s preserves the signed input algebraically (up to resize/FP rounding). Keeping aperture unchanged multiplies input magnitude by 1/s.",
    "Aperture0/.25/.5/1 probes establish finite runtime/control response, not a measured physical radius or selected K mapping.",
    "The training r_max, its output-resolution scaling and the private Any-to-Bokeh adapter remain unverified; retain K/32 as an explicit provisional UI-range assumption only."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Results concern the current CPU binaries/hardware and external-geometry graph, not native TF1 GPU parity.",
    "Out-of-range uint8 behavior must not be generalized to arbitrary devices; the local native and compat probes differ on identical values.",
    "No checkpoint, SR cast, gamma, source scene, GT or metric was changed. No benchmark-score search was performed."
  ]
